//RS /// #4318 §4: the root name of a loop source that is a plain place, `xs` or
//RS /// `a.b.xs`, possibly under a sema-inserted share copy (`Expr::Copy` whose
//RS /// span is its operand's: it lowers to `TExprKind::Clone`, which the walk
//RS /// drops). A user `~` copy (span starts at the sigil, lowers to
//RS /// `ExplicitCopy`), a call, or an index is not a stable source.
